s, acceptance evidence and rollout.","Verify complete inventory coverage and preserve inspection limitations separately from demonstrated artifact defects."],"dependsOn":["contracts","durability","observation","validation"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"Every inventory unit is assigned to at least one substantive chunk. Shared section selectors recur where identity, persistence, observation and validation responsibilities intersect. Diagram definitions, participants and generated companions are assigned together to durability. Chunks follow contract, storage, consumer and validation dependencies; the final consistency chunk depends on every substantive chunk.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["contracts"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["contracts"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["contracts","durability","observation"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["contracts","durability","observation"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["contracts","observation"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["contracts","durability","observation","validation"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["validation"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["validation"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["validation"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/body/companions","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice/ownedContracts/0","chunkIds":["contracts"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice/ownedContracts/1","chunkIds":["observation"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice/ownedContracts/2","chunkIds":["observation"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["contracts","validation"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["contracts"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["observation"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["contracts","validation"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["contracts","durability"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["contracts","observation"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["contracts"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["contracts"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["observation"]},{"unitId":"/citations/9","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"/citations/10","chunkIds":["durability","validation"]},{"unitId":"/citations/11","chunkIds":["observation"]},{"unitId":"/citations/12","chunkIds":["observation"]},{"unitId":"/citations/13","chunkIds":["contracts"]},{"unitId":"document:line:26","chunkIds":["contracts"]},{"unitId":"document:line:191","chunkIds":["durability"]},{"unitId":"document:line:195","chunkIds":["contracts","observation"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"contracts","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"durability","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"observation","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"validation","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"consolidated-chat-progress-s1-lld","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":6,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"contracts","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned scope, cardinalities, sibling responsibilities and fencing invariants align with the DEF and HLD. Two contract gaps remain: establishing trusted authorization bindings and defining the producer-to-coordinator ownership interface.","findings":[{"id":"contracts-01","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:80","message":"Authorization assumes a server-bound peer/session/project/origin tuple without specifying how ordinary IPC callers establish it or recover it after reconnect/restart. Current TrustedRpcContext provides connection identity and optional specialized connection sessions; the normal step host accepts cwd/envRepo/client from request parameters, and TargetRegistry routes by self-reported label/pid. These do not establish conversation ownership. Define trusted binding admission, authorized reattachment, revocation and project-history access after conversation removal, including which daemon component verifies each association. Otherwise the implementation must invent the security boundary required by s1/ac4.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:79-84","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:156","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:181","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:story s1/ac4","src/daemon/request-context.ts:12-24","src/daemon/server.ts:connectionContext and validClient","src/daemon/steps/host.ts:contextOf","src/daemon/threads/registry.ts:35-40"]},{"id":"contracts-02","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:44","message":"The shared producer interface specifies only progress(task), while ownership registration is merely a precondition. No contract defines admission inputs/results, owner-handle issuance, attempt rollover/revalidation, detail-validator registration, refresh signaling, or delivery of verified lifecycle/terminal evidence. DelegateMeasurement contains no lifecycle or terminal-result fields, so its only defined method cannot supply ProgressSnapshot.state or resultRef. The cancellation executor hook is also unspecified. Define the common owner/coordinator operations and their fencing/error semantics so s2–s4 can implement adapters against s1 without independently inventing incompatible ownership and lifecycle channels.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json:/body/hldContextSlice/ownedContracts/0/interfaceSketch",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json:/body/contractDetails/api","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:59","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:68","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:129","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:147","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md:Architecture shape","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md:Story boundaries s1–s4","src/daemon/steps/host.ts:StepToolRunner and createStepCallHandler","src/daemon/review-request-owner.ts:registerLocalReviewOwner"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/hldContextSlice/ownedContracts/0","/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/13","document:line:26","document:line:195","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/er-model.html:embedded relationship definition","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/review-evidence/er-model.png:actual rendering","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md:R1–R17","src/daemon/server.ts","src/daemon/request-context.ts","src/daemon/threads/registry.ts","src/daemon/threads/router.ts:dispatch and send","src/daemon/steps/host.ts","src/daemon/review-request-owner.ts","src/shared/types.ts:IPC and progress contracts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Replace citation c2's descriptive structural-map label with a retrievable bundle identifier or concrete source references."]},{"chunkId":"durability","status":"incomplete","summary":"The bounded per-task record approach supports atomic transitions, terminal publication ordering and fenced recovery. One capacity-recovery gap remains. Sequence source and generated content were inspected, but its actual rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"durability-01","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:169","message":"Storage reclamation covers terminal records only, while restart recovery can retain unknown attempts indefinitely without a returning owner. No transition defines when those records release active reservations, which quota subsequently owns them, or when their disk reservations expire. After repeated owner losses, unrevalidated records can exhaust active capacity or the global budget permanently because terminal-only eviction cannot reclaim them. Define bounded retention and reservation release for unrevalidated attempts, preserving an explicit unknown/expired outcome and rejecting late callbacks. Include a restart-and-capacity test proving that observation admission recovers without inventing execution termination.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json:/body/dataModelChanges/1",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json:/body/dataModelChanges/2","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:219","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md:7. Non-functional targets","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:s1/ac6"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/dataModelChanges","/body/contractDetails","/body/errorPaths","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/companions","/citations/4","/citations/9","/citations/10","document:line:191","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-s1-lld.json","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/sequence-diagram.html:Mermaid source, narrative and message descriptions","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/er-model.html:relationship source","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/review-evidence/er-model.png:actual rendering","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/review-evidence/visual-verification.md","src/workflow/storage.ts:writeAtomic","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/fixtures/task-persistence.ts","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:242"],"limitations":["Actual rendering of /body/sequenceDefinition and its /body/companions entry, docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/sequence-diagram.html, could not be inspected: the browser access host was unavailable, and no capture of this S001 companion was present. The available sequence capture documents the separate HLD companion. Source/content consistency was inspected, but visual verification remains incomplete."],"advice":["Separate terminal recovery from surviving-active-attempt recovery in the sequence narrative or diagram. Its current linear sequence delivers a terminal outcome and later revalidates a surviving attempt without identifying an alternate path or another task.","Clarify that citation c11 demonstrates temporary-session persistence exclusion, rather than crash-safe progress persistence. The proposed injected storage-failure fixtures must establish the latter independently."]},{"chunkId":"observation","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The observation, cancellation and activity invariants broadly align with the DEF and HLD. Observer isolation, durable cancel-pending ordering, verified terminal outcomes and separate activity clocks are preserved. The fallback scheduler contract remains insufficiently specified for its downstream adapter.","findings":[{"id":"observation-01","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:86","message":"Define the coordinator's observer and fallback-lease protocol. ObservationReply is a response shape with an undefined ObserverBinding parameter; no operation specifies how a consumer attaches, claims or renews scheduler ownership, claims a cadence slot, completes an in-flight slot, or transfers ownership. The record lists lease fields, but supplies neither a bounded scheduler lease lifetime nor renewal/expiry transitions. Consequently, s6 must invent how a disconnected holder becomes replaceable and how replies from its outstanding poll are rejected after transfer—the HLD explicitly requires both fencing and preservation of cadence. Specify request/result and error shapes, server-owned binding lifecycle, bounded expiry, transfer/in-flight fencing and terminal shutdown, then cover those transitions with deterministic clock tests. Concrete MCP presentation remains s6-owned.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:92","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:104","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:107","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:181","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:184","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:223","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md:41","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:k5","src/daemon/server.ts:261"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/hldContextSlice/ownedContracts/1","/body/hldContextSlice/ownedContracts/2","/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/citations/2","/citations/5","/citations/8","/citations/11","/citations/12","document:line:195","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-s1-lld.json","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md:R1–R16 and acceptance requirements","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/er-model.html:relationship source and descriptions","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/review-evidence/er-model.png:actual rendering","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/review-evidence/visual-verification.md:matching ER source hash","src/daemon/server.ts:trusted connection context and disconnect lifecycle","src/daemon/request-context.ts","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts","src/daemon/review-request-owner.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/coordinator.ts:owner, activity and execution fencing","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/controller.ts:activity validation and exchange ordering","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/checkpoint-progress.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/progress.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Replace citation c3's descriptive structural-map label with a retrievable evidence reference. The cited session-pool and review-ownership claims were independently checked against current code."]},{"chunkId":"validation","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned sections and citations were inspected. The additive rollout and sibling dependency ordering align with the HLD. The validation design lacks explicit coverage for activity expiry and capacity boundaries, and its predecessor traceability fixture assumes links absent from the cited documents.","findings":[{"id":"validation-01","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:247","message":"The proposed tests do not cover the foundation's activity-association lifecycle or its capacity boundaries. No subject verifies 30-second renewal and 120-second expiry without observers, rejection of observer-driven renewal, independent associations for multiple tasks, or conversation removal releasing only its association. Likewise, 'Recover bounded snapshots' does not specify saturation assertions for active/terminal/global reservations, full observer queues with terminal delivery, or admission failure preserving execution. These are explicit s1-owned correctness requirements, rather than client qualification work. Add deterministic lifecycle and boundary tests with expected outcomes, including late activity after expiry and visible observation refusal without cancelling or blocking the executor.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json:/body/testStrategy","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:2.5 TaskActivityLease","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:3.2 Durable observation and bounded replay","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:3.3 Runtime activity and fallback observer leases","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md:7. Non-functional targets","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts:155"]},{"id":"validation-02","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:254","message":"The ac5 proving test assumes a 'predecessor DEF with story links', but the actual predecessor DEF identifies S001–S003 without their tracker links, and the consolidated DEF only names #42–#44 collectively. The LLD supplies neither a concrete source-to-successor mapping nor a step to create the required traceability. Consequently, checking the two declared fixtures cannot establish the required identification and preservation of all three predecessor story records. Specify the traceability deliverable and assertions using the existing S001/#42, S002/#43 and S003/#44 records, map their requirements to successor scope, and preserve tracker disposition.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json:/body/testStrategy/testLevels/2","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:STORY-206db3426ffd4428-s1/ac5","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:k9","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md:Stories","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/S001/LLD.md:8","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/S002/LLD.md:8","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/S003/LLD.md:8"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/openQuestions","/body/errorPaths","/citations/0","/citations/3","/citations/10","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-s1-lld.json","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/S001/LLD.md:tracker header","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/S002/LLD.md:tracker header","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E