pdates acceptance mappings and predecessor fixtures.","Citations c15–c17 identify the three predecessor story records; the live document adds tracker #147 and shifts inventory document selectors.","Summary, HLD context slice, migration, alternatives, open questions, sequence definition and companion declaration are unchanged, but remain affected by the revised foundation semantics."],"directChunkIds":["contracts","durability","observation","validation"],"indirectChunkIds":[],"rationale":"Attempt 1 completed its review cycle with an incomplete aggregate result: contracts, observation and validation requested changes without limitations, while durability and consistency had mandatory S001 sequence-rendering limitations. Every current substantive chunk contains directly changed material, so full mode selects all four and fresh final consistency with no retained coverage. Producer admission and lifecycle changes affect unchanged sc1 sketches and downstream s2–s4 boundaries; grants affect sc2, reconnect, cancellation, history and persistence; recovery expiry affects sc3 retention, quotas and cursor behavior; scheduler fencing affects s6 consumption and terminal shutdown. These dependencies require reassessing unchanged requirements, ownership/cardinality, migration, alternatives and linked visuals against the current DEF/story/HLD. The unchanged S001 sequence still needs fresh consistency and actual-rendering inspection; the available HLD sequence capture cannot substitute for it. All six accepted findings remain effective until freshly inspected.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["contracts"],"currentIds":["contracts"],"explanation":"Same implementation responsibility, expanded to inspect new producer and trusted-admission contracts. Document selectors move from lines 26/195 to 27/261. Changed shared sections preclude retention."},{"priorIds":["durability"],"currentIds":["durability"],"explanation":"Same persistence and visual responsibility, expanded for recovery deadlines