erences. Its session and review-ownership claims were independently checked against current code."]},{"chunkId":"validation","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The revised strategy covers activity leases, capacity pressure, restart deadlines, authorization grants and scheduler transfer. The predecessor crosswalk preserves source requirements and separates tracker retirement. Migration remains additive and dependency order is feasible. One acceptance-test gap remains for measured-progress normalization.","findings":[{"id":"validation-03","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:333","message":"The ac1 mapping does not specify tests proving its central measured-progress behavior. Its mapped subjects cover asynchronous fencing, scheduler cadence and activity renewal, but none states assertions for independent meaningful revisions across two attempts, phase/count advancement with declared units, retained freshness/milestones, or identical measurements with newer sample timestamps leaving meaningful revision unchanged. Fallback narration suppression does not prove measurement normalization. An implementation could increment meaningful revision on every sample or omit measurement units while satisfying the listed assertions. Add concrete normalization cases that distinguish real phase/count changes from duplicate measurements, sample-time changes, reads and heartbeats, and verify task isolation and preserved measurement age.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:72","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md:3. Architecture shape","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:302","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/S001/LLD.md:319",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-206db3426ffd4428-s1.json:/body/testStrategy/acceptanceMapping/0"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/